Journey: Sign-in with TOTP MFA refuses wrong credentials and codes, and a signed-out session is not reused
Id: login-mfa
Tags: @portal @identity @smoke @security
Role: session-check
Risk: 5
Requirements: AUTH-1, AUTH-2, AUTH-3

# Wrong password
Open /login
  Expect the page contains "Sign in to MyCover"
Type "amelia.hart" into the Username field
Type "not-the-password" into the Password field
Click the "Sign in" button
  Expect the page contains "Incorrect username or password."
Expect the URL contains "/login"

# Right password, wrong one-time code
Type "amelia.hart" into the Username field
Type "${AMELIA_PASSWORD}" into the Password field
Click the "Sign in" button
  Expect the page contains "Two-step verification"
Type "000000" into the "Authentication code" field
Click the "Verify" button
  Expect the page contains "That code is not valid"
Expect the URL does not contain "/app/home"

# The Identity Vault signs in with the TOTP seed (secret://env/AMELIA_TOTP) and caches the session
Clear the browser state
Log in
Open /app/home
  Expect the page contains "Welcome, Amelia Hart"

# After signing out the server session is gone: the vault must notice and sign in again, not reuse a dead cookie
Click the "Sign out" link
  Expect the URL contains "/login"
Log in
Open /app/home
  Expect the page contains "Welcome, Amelia Hart"
